## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of event-driven AWS architectures, video processing workflows, and end-to-end data indexing, with emphasis on security, reliability, and cost optimization.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven orchestration using S3 event notifications and Step Functions
- AWS Elemental MediaConvert for multi-format video processing (MP4, GIF thumbnails)
- DynamoDB indexing with comprehensive video metadata
- Security best practices: IAM least privilege, encryption at rest and in transit, access logging
- Robust error handling: retry mechanisms, dead-letter queues, comprehensive monitoring
- Cost optimization strategies: appropriate resource sizing, storage lifecycle policies, and efficient processing patterns

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Lambda snippet: update DynamoDB after MediaConvert completion
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const { jobId, status, output } = event.detail;

  if (status === 'COMPLETE') {
    const params = {
      TableName: process.env.VIDEOS_TABLE,
      Item: {
        videoId: output.videoId,
        sourceKey: output.inputFile,
        thumbnailKey: output.thumbnailPath,
        previewKey: output.mp4Path,
        duration: output.duration,
        encodingQuality: '1080p',
        processedAt: new Date().toISOString()
      }
    };

    await ddb.put(params).promise();
  }
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of end-to-end AWS data pipelines using AI services, speaker diarization, secure data handling, error management, IAM least-privilege principles, and cost optimization for beginner-level implementations.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven architecture: S3 → Lambda → Amazon Transcribe → DynamoDB
- Transcribe diarization for per-speaker transcript segmentation
- Multi-format output storage (full + individual speaker transcripts)
- DynamoDB indexing strategy with composite keys
- IAM security with least-privilege access patterns
- Error handling with retries and dead-letter queues
- Data privacy through KMS encryption and access controls
- Cost monitoring and optimization for short audio clips

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Lambda: S3 event handling to start Transcribe
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const record = event.Records[0];
  const bucket = record.s3.bucket.name;
  const key = record.s3.object.key;

  // Start Transcribe job with diarization
  const transcribeParams = {
    TranscriptionJobName: `interview-${Date.now()}`,
    LanguageCode: 'en-US',
    MediaFormat: key.split('.').pop(),
    Media: { MediaFileUri: `s3://${bucket}/${key}` },
    Settings: {
      ShowSpeakerLabels: true,
      MaxSpeakerLabels: 10
    },
    OutputBucketName: process.env.OUTPUT_BUCKET
  };

  await transcribe.startTranscriptionJob(transcribeParams).promise();
};
```

